    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "title": "Filter",
            "content": [
                "Turn the air conditioner unit off prior to changing the air filter."
            ],
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/ClE6xHOQDRlNGIK5.medium",
            "images_200x150": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/5a6PkDLRGKpK322V.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/wmoasOcu2gV14Pq1.200x150"
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/147553/302373",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "content": [
                "Go into the attic where your air conditioner unit is located via the access door on the ceiling or wherever your air conditioner is located."
            ],
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/Kw4jW5v1WiRUIBDs.medium",
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/147553/302374",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "content": [
                "Open the filter access door and pull the old filter out."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/147553/302376",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "content": [
                "Examine your furnace to determine the air flow direction.",
                "The Return Duct",
                "The Furnace Unit",
                "**The air will always flow from the return duct towards the furnace unit.**",
                "Your old filter may also have an arrow indicator on the side.",
                "The arrow's direction will indicate the air flow direction."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/147553/302378",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 5,
            "content": [
                "Remove the old filter by pulling it out of the duct."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/147553/302382",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 6,
            "content": [
                "Insert the new filter.",
                "Pay attention to which direction the new filter should face before inserting it; make it is correct."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/147553/302383",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 7,
            "content": [
                "Reattach the filter cover.",
                "Ensure that the filter cover is securely in place."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/147553/302384",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 8,
            "content": [
                "Turn on the furnace.",
                "Flip the switch from the \"OFF\" position to the \"ON\" position."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/147553/302385",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": "This step-by-step guide aims to raise awareness about the importance of regular air filter replacement and provide clear instructions for a successful replacement process.",
